    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, we're having a major issue. the refrigeration unit on our main seafood transport truck just failed mid-route. the temp is climbing fast and we have a full load of high-end tuna. what are the immediate steps we need to take to minimize loss and what do i need to check regarding food safety protocols?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Firstly, ensure the truck is parked in a shaded area to prevent further internal temperature rise. Contact a roadside truck refrigeration repair service immediately. Do not attempt to drive the truck with its existing collapsed unit and check your service contract for coverage. Consult your temperature logs to ensure you meet delivery requirements as per food safety and traceability regulations. As soon as the truck is repaired, take the fish's temperature readings remotely and before opening the truck. If elevated, consider contacting the destination to explain the situation. Carry out a temperature history, and if needed, utilize any freeze packs or - hypothetic- portable cooling unit if it’s available in your fleet to bring the temperature back to the safe range for a short period until you can get professional help. Document the incident thoroughly for necessary reports and future reference. It’s critical to inform the destination of the situation and offer the best possible outcome.",
      "source": "target",
